---
title: Apply & Verify
---

With your feature flags edited and the build configuration regenerated, this step shows you how to rebuild the app and confirm your changes on an emulator or device.

## Rebuild and Run

Back on your machine, rebuild and relaunch the app:

{% steps %}

1. If you haven't already, run `./gradlew clean installDebug` from the project root (a full clean build ensures any product-flavor changes take effect).

2. Or in Android Studio, use **Build → Clean Project**, then press the ▶️ **Run** button (or **Shift+F10**) with your emulator or device selected.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" %}
If the app is still running from a previous build, stop it first before reinstalling — otherwise you may see stale behavior.
{% /aside %}

## Verify on the Emulator or Device

Join or start a meeting and check that your changes are reflected. Following the example from the previous step:

{% steps %}

1. Join a meeting room — confirm the initial layout matches your `defaultLayoutMode` setting (for example, a grid layout).

2. Check the in-call toolbar — confirm the screen-share button is hidden if you set `allowScreenShare` to `false`.

3. Try any other flags you changed — for example `allowChat`, `allowCaptions`, or `allowEmojis` — and confirm the corresponding UI element appears or disappears.

{% /steps %}

## Iterating Quickly

A typical configure-test cycle:

{% steps %}

1. Edit `config/app-config.json`.

2. Run `./gradlew generateVonageConfig`.

3. Run `./gradlew clean installDebug` (or Clean Project + Run in Android Studio).

4. Verify on the emulator or device.

{% /steps %}

Your feature flag configuration is live. Head to the final step for further resources.
